WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.084
- It was very important to us

00:00:01.084 --> 00:00:03.211
that you were seeing
various representations

00:00:03.211 --> 00:00:04.838
of what it is to be a woman.

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:06.047
In "Lessons In Chemistry,"

00:00:06.047 --> 00:00:07.841
there's so many examples on screen,

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:09.884
but then you also have it
behind the camera as well.

00:00:09.884 --> 00:00:12.554
(upbeat music)

00:00:12.554 --> 00:00:13.638
- Rolling!

00:00:13.638 --> 00:00:14.681
- Mark.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.558
- And...action!

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.686
- It's been so incredible
to walk onto these sets

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:23.773
where I have seen so many women in
producers and directors,

00:00:23.773 --> 00:00:26.735
to have that understanding
and to move forward together

00:00:26.735 --> 00:00:29.863
in this very daring way,
exposing our truths,

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:31.948
it's intensely wonderful.

00:00:32.574 --> 00:00:35.201
- It's nice to have
anyone tell this story,

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:37.579
but it brings a little
bit more when it's someone

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:40.248
who may have experienced similar
things in their own career.

00:00:40.248 --> 00:00:41.916
- Sweetheart, I could
use another cup of joe

00:00:41.916 --> 00:00:42.500
when you're done with that.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.919
- Most women on production
can understand trying

00:00:44.919 --> 00:00:47.547
to claw their way into
getting taken seriously,

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.467
so to have our directors who
are all women commanding a set,

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:52.010
it was really cool to see.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:53.887
- You're gonna be right here to go, boom.

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:57.891
- I'm Black female director in
a very male-oriented industry

00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:00.852
so I understood that battle of saying

00:01:00.852 --> 00:01:02.437
this is what I wanna
do, this is what I love,

00:01:02.437 --> 00:01:04.898
why can't I do it, why
is it different for me?

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:08.735
- We have rules, Miss Zott.
Who do you think you are?

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:09.360
- A woman.

00:01:09.819 --> 00:01:13.364
- When I started, there were
very few women around me.

00:01:13.364 --> 00:01:15.366
You just kind of realized early on

00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:18.036
that in order to get there,
you really have to be fierce,

00:01:18.036 --> 00:01:20.955
but at the same time, be more gentle

00:01:20.955 --> 00:01:22.457
because if you're not gentle as a woman,

00:01:22.457 --> 00:01:23.708
then you're considered a bitch.

00:01:23.708 --> 00:01:25.543
- How would you describe the host?

00:01:25.543 --> 00:01:31.966
Stuck up, unpleasant, didn't smile once.

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:34.302
- There's a beauty to Elizabeth Zott,

00:01:34.302 --> 00:01:35.887
but also good grittiness to her,

00:01:35.887 --> 00:01:37.931
and we all can relate to that.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:40.558
- Are those pants? Why
is she wearing pants?

00:01:40.558 --> 00:01:43.895
- Whether it's costumes or
production design or props,

00:01:43.895 --> 00:01:46.189
you're getting that experience
in every layer of it.

00:01:46.856 --> 00:01:48.399
- Knowing there’s
like two or three women

00:01:48.399 --> 00:01:50.777
or two or three people of
color in each department,

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:51.736
it makes it easier.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:56.241
- On this project, I really
felt heard and trusted.

00:01:56.241 --> 00:01:57.575
One ready to go for her to pull

00:01:57.575 --> 00:01:58.827
and then maybe she cuts into-

00:01:58.827 --> 00:02:01.079
- That's brilliant, Courtney.
- Yeah!

00:02:01.079 --> 00:02:04.415
- If you are the most
capable at doing something,

00:02:04.415 --> 00:02:06.376
you should get the opportunity to do it

00:02:06.376 --> 00:02:08.253
and excel at it, period.

00:02:08.253 --> 00:02:10.213
- Why would anyone
discriminate based on something

00:02:10.213 --> 00:02:12.757
as intellectually
non-determinative as gender?

00:02:12.757 --> 00:02:13.591
- Calvin,

00:02:15.343 --> 00:02:17.846
how many female scientists can you name?

00:02:17.846 --> 00:02:18.930
- Madam Curie?

00:02:20.265 --> 00:02:21.141
- Exactly.

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:22.725
- If you're gonna do this, this industry,

00:02:22.725 --> 00:02:25.395
or actually any industry, take up space.

00:02:25.395 --> 00:02:27.188
Take up space the best way you know how.

00:02:27.188 --> 00:02:29.023
Don't diminish yourself for others.

00:02:29.023 --> 00:02:32.318
- You have a platform, what you say matters.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.696
- The best piece of advice that I ever got

00:02:34.696 --> 00:02:37.866
was from a fellow filmmaker
who told me to just do you,

00:02:37.866 --> 00:02:41.119
and that changed my whole
perspective as a director.

00:02:41.119 --> 00:02:42.996
Let me just see how you would do it.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:45.331
- Pour it in and then
put it back on the flame,

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.708
tilting it slightly,

00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:48.751
and then it should just go up in flames.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.338
- Having women behind the camera,

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.549
it's just amazing to watch.

00:02:54.549 --> 00:02:57.635
And then I know it's gonna
empower some little girl.

00:02:57.635 --> 00:02:58.928
- I didn't know that it was possible

00:02:58.928 --> 00:03:00.889
for me to work in a camera department,

00:03:00.889 --> 00:03:03.683
and so for me to see these
women stand up and be like,

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:05.268
"Hey, I wanna bring the
camera over here," or,

00:03:05.268 --> 00:03:07.562
"Hey, I like this type of
shot," is super inspiring.

00:03:08.229 --> 00:03:09.647
- It's a really powerful feeling

00:03:09.647 --> 00:03:11.733
to know that we are all here

00:03:11.733 --> 00:03:13.651
because we wanna bring excellence to this,

00:03:13.651 --> 00:03:15.862
because we know the story deserves it,

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.780
and that we're capable of bringing it.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.741
- At the end of our time here together,

00:03:19.741 --> 00:03:21.743
we will have done something worth doing,

00:03:23.119 --> 00:03:23.995
and it will matter.

00:03:23.995 --> 00:03:27.081
(soft music)

